The provided class is a thin wrapper around a `Callable` that emits a single value via RxJava's `Observable`. Its behavior is straightforward and deterministic, with minimal internal logic (null check, error handling, and delegation). Such a simple utility typically does not warrant a dedicated JMH benchmark, as the performance characteristics are already well understood and any overhead is negligible compared to the work performed by the underlying `Callable`. Moreover, creating a benchmark for this specific class would add little value beyond existing RxJava performance tests.